// Boss encounter spec — the Inugami: Wolfenstein's head, torn off his dead
// body and risen as a red spirit (Jon, 2026-10-20). A boss of its own: its
// placement sleeps until his is cleared (`wakes_after` on the BossSpawn).
//
// Behaviour lives in `assets/data/boss_profiles.ron`; the conductor is
// `ambition_content_modules::inugami`.
//
// Music: silence while it waits in his body. As the seam round his neck pops,
// the theremin of his own march (a sting: `boss.inugami.unsewn_sting`, played
// by the conductor) cues that something is wrong with the head; when the head
// tears off, `iron_toccata` comes in under the rest of the rise and plays the
// whole fight (Jon, 2026-10-22: "I did like the theramin to cue the player
// into something being up with the head, but we should also probably start
// iron toccata a bit sooner", then "When it tears off").
(
    id: "wolfenstein_inugami",
    name: "Inugami",
    max_hp: 48,
    phase1_to_transition_hp: 0.5,
    phase2_to_enrage_hp: 0.2,
    // The rise (`ambition_content_modules::inugami`, `INTRO_S`): it waits in
    // his body while his death plays out, his head tears off, the fire catches
    // and it howls under its name.
    intro_seconds: 9.9,
    // It flares and howls, then crashes through the arena's wall on the way
    // out (`ambition_content_modules::inugami`, `FLARE_S`, `CRASH_SPEED`): the
    // wall breaks when its second phase starts, and it hunts you to the final
    // hall through the gap.
    transition_seconds: 2.4,
    music_intro: "iron_toccata",
    // His head tears off this long after the Inugami wakes, which is when he
    // dies: `ambition_content_modules::wolfenstein::HEAD_OFF_AT` (7.26 s).
    music_intro_from: 7.26,
    music_phase1: "iron_toccata",
    music_phase2: "iron_toccata",
    music_enrage: "iron_toccata",
    voice: Some("npc_wolfenstein_inugami"),
    // Its killing blow ends the whole fight: time hangs while it falls
    // (`ambition_boss_encounter::finish`).
    slow_motion_finish: true,
)
